  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 5.St Paul's Street
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: "227 St Paul\u2019s Street "
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.515485, y: 35.898254}
  firstPartInfo: "I manage to trace the first case: Salvatore Borg of St Paul\u2019s
    Street showed symptoms on the 3rd of May 1813 and was transferred to quarantine.
    Searching through the archives, I find out that Salvatore was registered as the
    first plague case but was, actually, not the first to contract the disease. His
    wife died prior to him, having caught the plague from their thirteen-year-old
    daughter, who was the true first victim despite the doctor not naming her as
    such. It seems that the Borg household was the epicentre of the pandemic spreading
    throughout Valletta, and the rest of Malta afterwards. But how did they contract
    the disease? Malta is sealocked, so the disease must have come via the sea. Salvatore
    Borg was a shoemaker, so he had no apparent contact with the port. According
    to testimonies of the time, Borg\u2019s last meeting was with two men who\u2019d
    sold him contraband linen. Where did this linen come from? How did these men
    come into possession of it?"
  secondPartInfo: "The answer is obviously a ship. A ship must have arrived at the
    shores of Malta carrying linen and the infectious disease. From then, it was
    fairly straightforward for the plague to reach the mainland and spread throughout
    the capital. But which ship was that and where did it dock? The port shouldn\u2019t
    be far away from the quarantine centre since this would be used mostly for people
    coming from outside Malta. Maybe I can reach another vantage point that will
    allow me to take a look from Valletta over to where the pestilence-laden fateful
    ship was to be docked. This time, though, I will not go high, but low. I will
    descend to sea level, to where boats still dock - not to go to other lands, but
    to take you to the town across the harbour."
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 6d0b91f615c65184982503f05fb75c42, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Quarantine
  hintOfPOI: "I know another place in Valletta where you can look over at Fort Manoel.
    I tend to go there with my friends and drink Cisk with Kinnie. It\u2019s very
    close to a canoe club."
  solutionOfPOI: "It\u2019s a good spot to people-watch since it\u2019s right next
    to where the ferry to Sliema docks."
